    "created_at": "2019-08-05T13:46:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-05T13:46:10Z",
    "body": "Why a superset? If I have interface X exposed to A and B, it seems reasonable to include a mixin Y into X that is exposed to A or B. It does seem reasonable to me that if there's no overlap the inclusion should be invalid.\r\n\r\n(Aside: it's always a little weird to me that we have this \"extended attribute\" concept that's sometimes really core to the infrastructure and sometimes rather optional when evaluating some IDL, but I guess that's how it is and changing that is a large-scale operation best postponed until we have something really good.)",
